1
00:00:01,733 --> 00:00:06,600
(Previously on...) My name is Suzuki Hajime,
a high school sophomore, and I love BL.

2
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:10,700
And right now, I'm using the
popular guy Serizawa as a model

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,233
to write a BL novel.

4
00:00:14,067 --> 00:00:15,567
It's definitely over here.

5
00:00:15,667 --> 00:00:18,300
Really? You said that yesterday too.

6
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,667
The "Serizawa Haruto"
written in this notebook...

7
00:00:21,767 --> 00:00:22,967
Is that about me?

8
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:24,567
Could it be that you like me, Suzuki?

9
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:26,200
I'm doomed.

10
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:27,067
I'm sorry.

11
00:00:27,167 --> 00:00:30,733
Even though I'm a
fudanshi, it's just a hobby.

12
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:33,300
It's not like I actually
have feelings for you.

13
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:38,367
So I've never looked at
you that way, Serizawa.

14
00:00:39,733 --> 00:00:40,867
I see.

15
00:00:40,967 --> 00:00:44,900
Then let me read the
novel you wrote, Suzuki.

16
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,133
Huh?

17
00:00:46,233 --> 00:00:47,067
Come on, please.

18
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:51,733
Let me be your very first reader.

19
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:57,133
And just like that, I started
letting Serizawa read my novel.

20
00:01:33,133 --> 00:01:34,733
Is that it?

21
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:40,533
Yeah... That's all I've written so far.

22
00:01:42,133 --> 00:01:45,933
Sorry... It's probably
not very good, is it?

23
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:50,300
But you stopped right at the part where
I really want to know what happens next!

24
00:01:51,333 --> 00:01:53,867
Does it actually read like a novel?

25
00:01:53,967 --> 00:01:54,967
Yeah.

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,567
Is the "uke" likable?

27
00:01:56,667 --> 00:01:58,533
Does the "seme" seem cool?

28
00:01:58,633 --> 00:02:01,133
Don't worry, I really like the uke too.

29
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:02,333
He's really cute.

30
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,567
Thank goodness...

31
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,233
Thank you, Serizawa.

32
00:02:08,333 --> 00:02:11,333
After all, the model for the
seme is pretty handsome.

33
00:02:11,433 --> 00:02:13,000
That's true.

34
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:16,200
So when are you going to write the rest?

35
00:02:16,299 --> 00:02:19,066
I usually write during
breaks between classes.

36
00:02:19,167 --> 00:02:21,000
Or little by little at home.

37
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,367
On this phone?

38
00:02:22,467 --> 00:02:23,333
Yeah.

39
00:02:23,433 --> 00:02:25,100
Hey...

40
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,900
Then write it right now.

41
00:02:27,967 --> 00:02:30,400
- Right now?
- Yeah, right now.

42
00:02:35,667 --> 00:02:37,600
I... I got it.

43
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:48,767
You want me to write
it right in front of you?

44
00:02:48,867 --> 00:02:51,267
Because I want to see what
happens next as soon as possible.

45
00:02:54,933 --> 00:02:56,833
I see...

46
00:03:03,467 --> 00:03:05,233
It's a bit hard to see.

47
00:03:06,367 --> 00:03:08,667
Ah, I know.

48
00:03:09,033 --> 00:03:10,800
Suzuki.

49
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:12,267
Sit here.

50
00:03:12,367 --> 00:03:13,700
Huh?

51
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,233
This way I can see the screen too.

52
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:19,633
But... isn't this a bit weird?

53
00:03:19,733 --> 00:03:20,733
What's weird about it?

54
00:03:20,833 --> 00:03:22,433
Not at all.

55
00:03:22,533 --> 00:03:23,900
Hurry up.

56
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:32,367
How is it? Comfortable?

57
00:03:32,967 --> 00:03:34,133
Not bad, right?

58
00:03:38,033 --> 00:03:39,767
It's not bad...

59
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:43,233
Alright, then for the sake of
your memorable first reader,

60
00:03:43,333 --> 00:03:47,167
please continue writing, Teacher Suzuki.

61
00:04:30,467 --> 00:04:33,433
"Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me"

62
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,433
(Episode 2)

63
00:04:36,533 --> 00:04:37,567
Um...

64
00:04:37,667 --> 00:04:39,067
Yeah?

65
00:04:39,167 --> 00:04:41,533
I still think this is really weird.

66
00:04:41,633 --> 00:04:42,467
What's weird about it?

67
00:04:42,567 --> 00:04:43,900
What do you mean, what's weird...

68
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,733
If someone sees us like this...

69
00:04:45,833 --> 00:04:47,000
Serizawa~.

70
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:49,100
We got the stuff you wanted.

71
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:51,633
Huh?

72
00:04:51,733 --> 00:04:53,813
- Bentos, bentos are here!
- What are you guys doing?

73
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:54,833
Ah... uh...

74
00:04:54,933 --> 00:04:56,433
Oh? That's weird.

75
00:04:56,533 --> 00:04:57,300
Suzuki.

76
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:59,500
- Hey~
- Ah...

77
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:02,000
How did he get captured?

78
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:03,833
I didn't capture him.

79
00:05:03,933 --> 00:05:04,667
Huh?

80
00:05:04,767 --> 00:05:07,000
We're just bonding, okay?

81
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:09,300
It totally looks like Serizawa
is just messing around.

82
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:10,800
No, I'm not.

83
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:12,600
Right, Suzuki?

84
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:16,400
Ah... um... no...

85
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:18,167
Ah... uh...

86
00:05:18,267 --> 00:05:19,800
Anyway, I'm starving~.

87
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:20,433
Let's eat already.

88
00:05:20,533 --> 00:05:23,200
Let's fill our stomachs.

89
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:25,333
I've been looking forward to this all day.

90
00:05:25,433 --> 00:05:28,833
- Yay~
- Can't wait.

91
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:30,567
Looks delicious.

92
00:05:30,667 --> 00:05:31,700
- What is it?
- Let's see.

93
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,943
Did your girlfriend make it again today?

94
00:05:32,967 --> 00:05:34,100
What?

95
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,000
I'm digging in.

96
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:36,700
Hey!

97
00:05:37,233 --> 00:05:41,433
Ah, um, Serizawa, I
should probably get going...

98
00:05:41,533 --> 00:05:42,933
Suzuki.

99
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,567
Here.

100
00:05:45,667 --> 00:05:47,333
Huh? For me?

101
00:05:47,433 --> 00:05:49,967
Don't worry, we bought some for you too.

102
00:05:50,067 --> 00:05:51,176
We're the ones who bought it.

103
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,967
But I'm the one who paid for it.

104
00:05:54,067 --> 00:05:55,307
Just wanted to make that clear.

105
00:05:55,367 --> 00:05:58,633
There he goes again, acting all high
and mighty over something so basic.

106
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:00,933
Classic Serizawa.

107
00:06:01,667 --> 00:06:02,709
Suzuki, which one do you want?

108
00:06:02,733 --> 00:06:03,167
So good.

109
00:06:03,267 --> 00:06:07,200
I figured I'd get you
both bread and a rice ball.

110
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:11,000
Then... I'll take the rice ball.

111
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:12,367
Okay.

112
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,467
Here you go.

113
00:06:14,567 --> 00:06:16,500
Ah... thanks.

114
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,567
I'll pay you back later.

115
00:06:18,667 --> 00:06:20,033
It's on me today.

116
00:06:20,133 --> 00:06:22,733
Consider it a treat for
Teacher Suzuki's hard work.

117
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:24,867
- Teacher?
- Wait a minute, Serizawa!

118
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:26,200
I know, I know.

119
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:30,033
What I just said is a secret
between Suzuki and me.

120
00:06:30,133 --> 00:06:31,500
Gross~.

121
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,760
Serizawa, you're so annoying.

122
00:06:32,833 --> 00:06:34,033
Seriously annoying.

123
00:06:34,133 --> 00:06:34,800
Right?
Oh, by the way...

124
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:36,633
What's that?

125
00:06:36,733 --> 00:06:38,243
- Is that fried chicken?
- Huh? Fried chicken?

126
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:38,800
Eat up.

127
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:39,900
Come on.

128
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,167
Hey, Serizawa.

129
00:06:41,267 --> 00:06:41,767
Yeah?

130
00:06:41,867 --> 00:06:43,033
Can I have a word with you?

131
00:06:43,133 --> 00:06:44,333
Sure.

132
00:06:44,433 --> 00:06:45,333
Does this taste like crab sticks?

133
00:06:45,433 --> 00:06:46,509
Doesn't really seem like it.

134
00:06:46,533 --> 00:06:48,067
But it's really good.

135
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:51,333
What's up?

136
00:06:51,433 --> 00:06:52,767
What's wrong?

137
00:06:53,933 --> 00:06:56,100
I just wanted to make sure.

138
00:06:57,567 --> 00:06:59,533
You didn't tell everyone, did you?

139
00:06:59,633 --> 00:07:03,333
You know... about me liking BL.

140
00:07:03,433 --> 00:07:06,833
Oh, yeah, I didn't say anything.

141
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,667
Thank goodness...

142
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:13,067
But I don't think they'd care anyway.

143
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:15,700
No, no, you absolutely can't tell them!

144
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:20,367
Alright, if you don't want
me to say anything, I won't.

145
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:24,133
Then it'll be our little secret.

146
00:07:25,367 --> 00:07:27,533
Yeah, thank you.

147
00:07:35,733 --> 00:07:37,333
But in return...

148
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:42,267
You have to eat lunch with
me every day from now on.

149
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,100
Huh? Every day?

150
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:48,033
Yeah, because I want to
read your novel every day.

151
00:07:48,933 --> 00:07:51,633
Please, Teacher Suzuki.

152
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,800
And just like that,

153
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,900
a week has passed since then.

154
00:08:00,433 --> 00:08:03,600
I wonder which one will
come first, it's hard to guess.

155
00:08:04,167 --> 00:08:09,033
I've been eating lunch with
these popular guys every day.

156
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:12,700
Here, Suzuki.

157
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,567
Say ah~.

158
00:08:17,667 --> 00:08:20,400
Or rather, I'm basically being spoon-fed.

159
00:08:21,333 --> 00:08:22,733
Is it good?

160
00:08:23,433 --> 00:08:25,000
It is good, but...

161
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:29,900
- No, seriously, what is going on here?
- This is ridiculous.

162
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,133
This is definitely still weird, Serizawa.

163
00:08:32,233 --> 00:08:35,100
Come on, just focus on writing, Suzuki.

164
00:08:35,633 --> 00:08:36,767
Here.

165
00:08:36,867 --> 00:08:38,367
Say ah~.

166
00:08:43,833 --> 00:08:46,400
By the way, what exactly is
Suzuki being forced to do?

167
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:48,600
Did you get blackmailed or something?

168
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:51,667
Are you okay? If you don't want to do it,
you really need to tell us.

169
00:08:51,767 --> 00:08:53,700
This guy is a total brat.

170
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:56,533
Shh, don't bother him!

171
00:08:56,633 --> 00:08:59,033
This is the "Serizawa
System" I specially developed

172
00:08:59,133 --> 00:09:02,133
to boost Suzuki's efficiency.

173
00:09:02,233 --> 00:09:03,400
Huh?

174
00:09:06,667 --> 00:09:08,200
What the heck is the Serizawa System?

175
00:09:08,833 --> 00:09:12,233
Besides, I can't help but feel...

176
00:09:12,867 --> 00:09:15,233
Serizawa is acting a bit weird.

177
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,633
Alright, let's start warming up.

178
00:09:21,733 --> 00:09:24,900
Suzuki, let's hang out today too.

179
00:09:29,033 --> 00:09:30,033
Suzuki.

180
00:09:30,967 --> 00:09:32,433
Let's walk home together.

181
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:42,000
I'm going this way, see you tomorrow.

182
00:09:43,267 --> 00:09:44,633
Suzuki.

183
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:47,600
Let's add each other as friends.

184
00:09:49,967 --> 00:09:52,667
It's definitely weird.

185
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,867
I ended up spending the whole day
with Serizawa again today.

186
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:11,733
Suzuki, are you asleep?
Wanna chat for a bit?

187
00:10:13,167 --> 00:10:16,300
Chat? Like, on the phone?

188
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:18,820
Don't tell me he wants to video call!?

189
00:10:22,567 --> 00:10:25,900
No, no, what should I do...

190
00:10:29,533 --> 00:10:33,933
Good night, Suzuki. See you tomorrow.

191
00:10:37,567 --> 00:10:41,833
Come to think of it, why is Serizawa so...

192
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:44,133
obsessed with hanging out with me?

193
00:10:45,933 --> 00:10:48,233
Should I reply to him...

194
00:10:50,633 --> 00:10:52,533
But... no.

195
00:10:54,767 --> 00:10:56,333
I don't get it.

196
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:14,467
Good morning, Teacher Suzuki.

197
00:11:14,567 --> 00:11:15,667
You scared me!

198
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:17,267
Good morning, Serizawa.

199
00:11:17,367 --> 00:11:18,767
Morning.

200
00:11:19,667 --> 00:11:21,467
You look really sleepy.

201
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Uh...

202
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:24,100
Yeah.

203
00:11:25,467 --> 00:11:27,700
I couldn't sleep at all
last night for some reason.

204
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:30,133
So I ended up... reading
until the middle of the night.

205
00:11:30,233 --> 00:11:32,633
What the heck? You were
actually awake last night?

206
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:34,933
Sorry! Even though you texted me.

207
00:11:35,033 --> 00:11:36,767
Did you need something?

208
00:11:37,333 --> 00:11:39,433
Not really, just...

209
00:11:39,533 --> 00:11:41,767
I just wanted to hear your voice.

210
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:42,700
Huh?

211
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:45,367
Oh, by the way, we
have cooking class today.

212
00:11:45,467 --> 00:11:47,133
I get to cook with Suzuki.

213
00:11:47,233 --> 00:11:48,667
I can't wait.

214
00:11:54,767 --> 00:11:56,767
Um, Serizawa...

215
00:11:56,867 --> 00:11:58,267
Yeah?

216
00:12:00,367 --> 00:12:01,833
Never mind...

217
00:12:04,167 --> 00:12:05,800
Suzuki, wait up!

218
00:12:07,567 --> 00:12:12,000
All right, today we're making stew.

219
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,800
Stew.

220
00:12:14,467 --> 00:12:15,800
Are all the ingredients ready?

221
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:16,467
All set.

222
00:12:16,567 --> 00:12:19,467
Okay, let's all...

223
00:12:28,167 --> 00:12:30,000
Serizawa, what's wrong?

224
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:34,300
Hey, Suzuki.

225
00:12:35,126 --> 00:12:38,593
I'm seen as an affectionate seme, right?

226
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:39,967
Huh?!

227
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:50,067
Well... at least in my mind you are.

228
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:53,900
I was just thinking,

229
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:58,200
aren't semes usually great at cooking?

230
00:12:59,167 --> 00:13:02,600
Yeah, that's true.

231
00:13:04,967 --> 00:13:08,167
All right, leave it to me, Suzuki.

232
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:11,767
I'm going to be the Stew King!

233
00:13:12,033 --> 00:13:13,033
Huh?

234
00:13:14,967 --> 00:13:16,433
What are you talking about?

235
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,267
Watch this.

236
00:13:23,967 --> 00:13:25,633
You didn't even twist it.

237
00:13:25,733 --> 00:13:28,033
Serizawa, how long is this going to take?

238
00:13:28,133 --> 00:13:29,900
Takeuchi, you're amazing at this.

239
00:13:30,667 --> 00:13:31,400
- It's a piece of cake.
- So fast.

240
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,033
Whoa, are you a pro?

241
00:13:33,133 --> 00:13:33,867
I told you it's easy.

242
00:13:33,967 --> 00:13:36,007
I should be asking how
you messed it up this badly.

243
00:13:46,167 --> 00:13:49,133
It's all stuck together, Serizawa.

244
00:13:49,233 --> 00:13:51,133
Wait, don't we need green onions?

245
00:13:51,233 --> 00:13:53,333
- Huh?
- We don't need those.

246
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,233
Then why did you bring them?

247
00:13:55,333 --> 00:13:56,833
- Hmm?
- Huh?

248
00:14:03,433 --> 00:14:04,767
A pencil?

249
00:14:04,867 --> 00:14:07,000
This guy really has zero talent.

250
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:09,267
Some Stew King you are, Serizawa.

251
00:14:10,567 --> 00:14:12,967
Tag... tag out, Serizawa.

252
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:18,267
Looks like you've got a long way to go.

253
00:14:18,367 --> 00:14:20,067
About 3,000 miles, maybe?

254
00:14:20,867 --> 00:14:22,033
Uh... he sat down.

255
00:14:22,133 --> 00:14:23,333
He's totally crushed.

256
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:25,320
Weren't you going to be the Stew King?

257
00:14:25,367 --> 00:14:26,033
Come on!
Don't give up!

258
00:14:27,033 --> 00:14:28,433
Get up!

259
00:14:31,233 --> 00:14:32,393
No, I think I'm a lost cause.

260
00:14:32,467 --> 00:14:33,633
Yeah.

261
00:14:37,533 --> 00:14:39,167
Let's dig in.

262
00:14:39,267 --> 00:14:41,200
Time to eat...

263
00:14:43,333 --> 00:14:44,733
Let's eat!

264
00:14:45,167 --> 00:14:46,167
Ready.

265
00:14:46,233 --> 00:14:46,933
Delicious.

266
00:14:47,033 --> 00:14:48,600
So good.

267
00:14:51,467 --> 00:14:52,300
Hmm?

268
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:53,800
Yeah, it's great.

269
00:14:54,933 --> 00:14:57,733
The broth Suzuki made is amazing.

270
00:14:57,833 --> 00:14:59,067
Yeah.

271
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:04,300
The carrots Suzuki cut
are the perfect size, too.

272
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:08,200
Thank God we have Suzuki.

273
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:10,467
Yeah.

274
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:14,567
Listen up, you guys.

275
00:15:14,667 --> 00:15:16,700
If you keep nagging me like this,

276
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,333
I'm quitting the group
over creative differences.

277
00:15:19,433 --> 00:15:20,167
I'm out right now.

278
00:15:20,267 --> 00:15:22,700
You were never even in the group, okay?

279
00:15:23,067 --> 00:15:24,633
Serizawa, you're so annoying.

280
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:28,333
Saeki, come here for a sec.

281
00:15:28,433 --> 00:15:30,100
The stew Koharu made is super good.

282
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,533
It's nothing, really.

283
00:15:31,633 --> 00:15:32,967
- Let me try some.
- It's fine...

284
00:15:33,067 --> 00:15:34,633
- Let's all share it.
- No, don't...

285
00:15:34,733 --> 00:15:36,733
It's embarrassing, stop it.

286
00:15:36,833 --> 00:15:39,300
- Time to dig in.
- Wait, don't just take it.

287
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,560
- Don't eat it all.
- Hold on.

288
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:46,267
Sorry, Suzuki.

289
00:15:47,667 --> 00:15:49,100
For what?

290
00:15:50,133 --> 00:15:53,367
Even though I'm an affectionate seme,

291
00:15:53,467 --> 00:15:55,367
I'm terrible at cooking.

292
00:15:56,767 --> 00:16:00,033
It's fine... You don't need
to worry about it so much.

293
00:16:00,867 --> 00:16:02,400
But...

294
00:16:02,733 --> 00:16:05,233
I want to be the ideal seme.

295
00:16:07,733 --> 00:16:15,300
Uh... it's not too
late to start learning.

296
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:16,900
Start learning now?

297
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,833
- Yeah.
- Because, you know,

298
00:16:18,933 --> 00:16:20,333
even the best semes out there...

299
00:16:20,433 --> 00:16:22,767
they all had to practice to get good at it.

300
00:16:23,367 --> 00:16:24,867
So...

301
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:27,933
Can I still become the Stew King?

302
00:16:28,033 --> 00:16:29,067
Yeah.

303
00:16:29,167 --> 00:16:31,567
I'm sure you can, Serizawa.

304
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:33,967
So don't be so down on yourself.

305
00:16:34,067 --> 00:16:35,400
Okay?

306
00:16:40,333 --> 00:16:41,067
Sorry...

307
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:43,067
I sounded like a know-it-all just now...

308
00:16:43,367 --> 00:16:44,767
Not at all.

309
00:16:46,667 --> 00:16:48,733
Thanks, Suzuki.

310
00:16:49,867 --> 00:16:51,733
I feel totally pumped up now.

311
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:56,233
Oh.

312
00:16:56,333 --> 00:16:57,833
That's good.

313
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:00,700
Oh, right.

314
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:03,100
Let's take a picture to commemorate this.

315
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,433
A picture?

316
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:06,940
A group shot of the
three of us with the stew.

317
00:17:07,533 --> 00:17:09,200
The stew?

318
00:17:14,433 --> 00:17:15,933
Here we go.

319
00:17:17,067 --> 00:17:18,833
Say cheese!

320
00:17:20,533 --> 00:17:21,733
Let's take one more.

321
00:17:24,967 --> 00:17:26,733
Say cheese!

322
00:17:36,267 --> 00:17:39,667
Cooking class was super fun,

323
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:42,076
but I didn't get any time
to read Suzuki's novel today.

324
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:43,833
It's such a bummer.

325
00:17:48,587 --> 00:17:49,753
I see...

326
00:17:51,339 --> 00:17:52,839
Yeah.

327
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:00,400
Thanks for today.

328
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,500
I'll work hard to become the Stew King.

329
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:09,400
The one Serizawa is interested in

330
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:12,033
is definitely not me.

331
00:18:13,867 --> 00:18:17,967
I can't wait to read the
next chapter tomorrow.

332
00:18:29,139 --> 00:18:31,879
(Story Outline)

333
00:18:36,133 --> 00:18:38,053
- Rock, paper, scissors!
- Rock, paper, scissors!

334
00:18:40,867 --> 00:18:43,633
Suzuki, let's walk home
together again today.

335
00:18:44,267 --> 00:18:45,533
Sure.

336
00:18:52,667 --> 00:18:54,967
Um, Serizawa.

337
00:18:55,067 --> 00:18:56,400
Yeah?

338
00:18:58,333 --> 00:19:02,833
There's something I want to tell you.

339
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,867
Okay.

340
00:19:17,967 --> 00:19:19,333
Serizawa...

341
00:19:20,833 --> 00:19:22,133
I'm sorry...

342
00:19:23,833 --> 00:19:27,933
Wh... what's wrong?

343
00:19:30,267 --> 00:19:34,600
That novel you're reading right now...

344
00:19:37,100 --> 00:19:38,800
I...

345
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:41,300
I might not be able to finish it.

346
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,567
Huh?

347
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:47,700
Actually, I...

348
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:49,133
(Story Outline)

349
00:19:51,567 --> 00:19:53,800
I've never once

350
00:19:54,233 --> 00:19:56,100
finished writing a novel.

351
00:19:58,267 --> 00:20:00,633
When I'm writing all by myself,

352
00:20:01,467 --> 00:20:04,233
I gradually start to lose track of

353
00:20:04,867 --> 00:20:07,133
whether I'm actually
interested in it or not...

354
00:20:07,867 --> 00:20:10,133
I always end up giving up halfway through.

355
00:20:12,567 --> 00:20:14,433
So this time, too...

356
00:20:14,533 --> 00:20:16,733
If I end up giving up halfway again,

357
00:20:17,767 --> 00:20:20,000
I'd feel terrible for letting you down.

358
00:20:24,267 --> 00:20:25,900
I...

359
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:30,500
I really don't deserve to be called teacher
nor having you read my novel, either.

360
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:36,200
What the heck? So that's what this is about.

361
00:20:37,133 --> 00:20:38,367
Huh?

362
00:20:38,467 --> 00:20:40,700
You scared me to death.

363
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:42,800
I thought it was because
I was so bad at cooking

364
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:45,967
that you decided I wasn't
fit to be a affectionate seme.

365
00:20:46,367 --> 00:20:47,733
Huh?

366
00:20:48,433 --> 00:20:52,167
But seriously, you really are amazing,

367
00:20:52,267 --> 00:20:53,500
Suzuki.

368
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:58,833
Because even though you've failed
and lost confidence time and time again,

369
00:20:58,933 --> 00:21:00,933
you're still here right now,

370
00:21:01,033 --> 00:21:03,633
still challenging yourself
over and over, right?

371
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:07,933
Isn't that incredible?

372
00:21:11,567 --> 00:21:13,100
Besides...

373
00:21:17,667 --> 00:21:21,167
you're not alone anymore.

374
00:21:22,067 --> 00:21:23,433
Huh?

375
00:21:25,133 --> 00:21:26,433
Hey, Suzuki.

376
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:31,133
If you ever get stuck while
writing by yourself again,

377
00:21:31,233 --> 00:21:32,633
just come to me.

378
00:21:33,967 --> 00:21:37,067
I'll rush over to you anytime, anywhere.

379
00:21:37,167 --> 00:21:39,233
I'll point out all the
amazing parts of your novel,

380
00:21:39,333 --> 00:21:40,976
and all the parts that
make my heart flutter.

381
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,176
I'll keep telling you until
you finally get it yourself.

382
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,933
I'll explain every single detail to you.

383
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:50,600
Serizawa...

384
00:21:52,133 --> 00:21:54,233
All right, it's a promise.

385
00:22:11,467 --> 00:22:12,467
Okay.

386
00:22:12,567 --> 00:22:15,300
Then I'll work hard to
become the Stew King, too.

387
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:17,267
Huh? You're serious?

388
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:19,900
I'm always serious.

389
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:21,200
Ah...

390
00:22:22,033 --> 00:22:24,533
Come on, show me your determination.

391
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:27,633
Huh? Why?

392
00:22:27,733 --> 00:22:29,443
Wait... hold on, that's
embarrassing! Delete it!

393
00:22:29,467 --> 00:22:30,333
No way!

394
00:22:30,433 --> 00:22:31,833
There you go again, Mr. Stubborn.

395
00:22:31,933 --> 00:22:32,943
Serizawa, you're so annoying.

396
00:22:32,967 --> 00:22:33,400
Suzuki?

397
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:34,533
Eh...

398
00:22:34,633 --> 00:22:36,033
Matsuno, what's wrong?

399
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:37,633
Ah...

400
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:40,700
Huh? Suzuki?

401
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,033
Is that Serizawa with him?

402
00:22:43,133 --> 00:22:45,333
Why the hell is Suzuki
hanging out with Serizawa?

403
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,633
Not giving it to you.

404
00:22:50,733 --> 00:22:52,300
Come on, just delete it already!

405
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:53,300
- Hurry up!
- Nope.

406
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,400
- Delete it!
- No.

407
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:55,533
- Delete it!
- No way.

408
00:22:55,633 --> 00:22:57,000
Jeez.

409
00:22:57,100 --> 00:22:58,000
What should I do?
Not a chance.

410
00:22:58,900 --> 00:22:59,933
I don't want to.

411
00:23:00,033 --> 00:23:01,043
(Next Episode Preview)
By the way, Suzuki...

412
00:23:01,067 --> 00:23:03,809
(The Definition of a Friend) When did you
get so close to Serizawa and the others?

413
00:23:03,833 --> 00:23:05,000
Finally found you.

414
00:23:05,100 --> 00:23:06,633
Wanna go to karaoke with everyone?

415
00:23:06,733 --> 00:23:09,133
I've never sung in front of people before.

416
00:23:09,233 --> 00:23:10,500
Are you serious?

417
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:13,509
(This drama is a work of fiction)
But I feel like I can sing right now.

418
00:23:13,533 --> 00:23:14,733
Sorry, I really can't do this.
